==Battleground==
*1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns.
*3 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*4 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.
**3 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn after 5.33 seconds<sup>160f</sup>, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.
**5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**3 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.
**2 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A shockingly easy stage compared to the others in Hunter's Map IV. While you do need to build your lineup with the followup stage in mind, there is little to worry about here. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] helps versus everything, [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] and [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]] demolish Rangmaster even without Shield Piercers, and attackers like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] perform well against Shadow Boxer Ks and Ragin' Gories.

